 "description": "The SAFE-Key device is a USB-based hardware security token; its primary purpose is two-factor authentication. The device supports three modalities: web-based two-factor authentication (patented), two-factor authentication for protected file decryption and two-factor authentication for digital signature generation. The two factors are something you have (i.e. a specific SAFE-Key device) and something you know (i.e. a password). It also supports one-factor, something you have (i.e. a specific SAFE-Key device) authentication.",
